From 96459440f92007b0c2455468e6a9f21ddea2ba5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:43:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] Round 3: Serialize typed record metrics instead of JSON
 value trees

The domain now returns a typed Metrics enum (skipped, property state,
cycle) whose struct fields are declared in sorted key order, and records
serialize it directly. This removes about a hundred map and string
allocations per full record while keeping the JSON byte-identical.
Failure diagnostics keep their optional serde_json::Value.

Workload: serial (96 full records, one worker), full API both sides.
Official 11-sample run: 1.482 ms -> 0.805 ms, 1.84x (paired 1.61x).
41-sample confirmation: 1.311 ms -> 0.791 ms, paired 1.66x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
